==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|k|a}}

===Etymology===
An old Baltic loan; derived from the same word from which e.g. Lithuanian {{term|gaũras}} is descended. Cognates include Veps and Estonian {{term|karv}} and Livonian {{term|kōra}}. Originally ''karva'' only had the meaning "color". In its current meaning it is first mentioned in a biblical text in 1621.<ref>{{cite book | last = Häkkinen | first = Kaisa | year = 2004 | title = Nykysuomen etymologinen sanakirja | publisher = WSOY | id = ISBN 951-0-27108-X }}</ref>

